\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Posterior inclusion probabilities (PIP) for the 12 NHANES features under SFRM (left) and LFRM (right). The most prominent discordance is smoking: PIP \(\approx 0\) under SFRM versus PIP \(= 0.324\) under LFRM, consistent with its locally discriminant role in a subset of clusters. Height also drops from PIP \(= 0.985\) (SFRM) to PIP \(= 0.461\) (LFRM), falling below the selection threshold.}}{12}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-nhanes-pips}{{3}{12}{Posterior inclusion probabilities (PIP) for the 12 NHANES features under SFRM (left) and LFRM (right). The most prominent discordance is smoking: PIP \(\approx 0\) under SFRM versus PIP \(= 0.324\) under LFRM, consistent with its locally discriminant role in a subset of clusters. Height also drops from PIP \(= 0.985\) (SFRM) to PIP \(= 0.461\) (LFRM), falling below the selection threshold}{figure.caption.10}{}}
